\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Time-expanded controller schedule produced by the exact program. Each row is an intersection; each block is a signal setting in effect at time $t$ (80\,s cycle, 35\,s bus-phase green, offsets staggered by 10\,s per intersection to form the green wave for the timetabled direction). Overlays show how the schedule \emph  {changes the controller settings in time}; the five numbered callouts are keyed beneath the axis (1 Green Extension $+10$\,s, 2 Phase Insertion $+15$\,s, 3 Early Red $-10$\,s, 4 Green Reallocation $\pm 10$\,s, 5 offset correction $-5$\,s). Callouts 1--3 steer the actual bus trajectory (red) back onto the timetable arrivals (circles) after a $+25$\,s queue delay. The opposing-direction bus (orange) cannot use the one-way stagger, so the strategy rotates the phase order wherever the stagger strands it (ROT windows at intersections 10, 7, 6 and 3, white tags): the bus approach takes the cross-street slot and the cross phase is deferred, cutting the return-trip red waits from 75\,s (gray counterfactual: held to 170 at row 10 and to 230 at row 8) to short slowdowns, and the bus rejoins regular greens at rows 8, 5 and 4. Callout~4 (violet) starts the bus green 10\,s early at intersection 5 while shortening the donor cross phase by the same amount, leaving the cycle sum unchanged; callout~5 shifts the downstream green start 5\,s earlier at intersection 11 to restore progression.}}{13}{figure.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:sched}{{2}{13}{Time-expanded controller schedule produced by the exact program. Each row is an intersection; each block is a signal setting in effect at time $t$ (80\,s cycle, 35\,s bus-phase green, offsets staggered by 10\,s per intersection to form the green wave for the timetabled direction). Overlays show how the schedule \emph {changes the controller settings in time}; the five numbered callouts are keyed beneath the axis (1 Green Extension $+10$\,s, 2 Phase Insertion $+15$\,s, 3 Early Red $-10$\,s, 4 Green Reallocation $\pm 10$\,s, 5 offset correction $-5$\,s). Callouts 1--3 steer the actual bus trajectory (red) back onto the timetable arrivals (circles) after a $+25$\,s queue delay. The opposing-direction bus (orange) cannot use the one-way stagger, so the strategy rotates the phase order wherever the stagger strands it (ROT windows at intersections 10, 7, 6 and 3, white tags): the bus approach takes the cross-street slot and the cross phase is deferred, cutting the return-trip red waits from 75\,s (gray counterfactual: held to 170 at row 10 and to 230 at row 8) to short slowdowns, and the bus rejoins regular greens at rows 8, 5 and 4. Callout~4 (violet) starts the bus green 10\,s early at intersection 5 while shortening the donor cross phase by the same amount, leaving the cycle sum unchanged; callout~5 shifts the downstream green start 5\,s earlier at intersection 11 to restore progression}{figure.caption.14}{}}
\newlabel{fig:sched@cref}{{[figure][2][]2}{[1][12][]13}}
